<title>JAPAN: Japan Energy Corp says minor oil spill contained.</title>
<headline>Japan Energy Corp says minor oil spill contained.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Refiner Japan Energy Corp said on Wednesday that a minor oil spill earlier in the day from one of its coastal tankers had been contained.</p>
<p>A company spokesman said the incident occurred at Japan Energy&quot;s Mizushima refinery in Okayama prefecture, southern Japan, at around 3.55 p.m. JST (0655 GMT) while loading fuel oil C onto a tanker for Kyushu Electric Power Co Inc.</p>
<p>The size of the spill could not immediately be confirmed, the spokesman said.</p>
<p>He quoted the Maritime Safety Agency as saying the spill would not threaten the environment.</p>
</text>
